

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 8

                                  FOR

                            GIOVANNA D'ARCO







          Alberto Clerici
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  "It is a political error to practice deceit, if deceit is carried too 
far."
  -Frederick II, King of Prussia, 1740.


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Giovanna d'Arco cast a Bless spell.  Sherwood was magically 
blessed and prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 142nd Legion were 
Blessed and permanently destroyed.  The skeletal remains of the 221st 
Light Cavalry were Blessed and permanently destroyed.
  During early summer, Giovanna d'Arco tried hard to improve her Meleeing, 
but she practiced in vain.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  Giovanna d'Arco 
marched on Tigerhome (#1702) with her command.
  With the coming of the fall season, Giovanna d'Arco searched the Cavern 
with the intention of prevailing over it and whatever guardian lay within 
it.  Giovanna d'Arco encountered the Black Dragon.  Incanting a Spiritwrack 
spell, Giovanna d'Arco channelled scintillating, interlacing strands of 
magic, to make the Black Dragon quake and shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  The Black Dragon cautiously advanced to bow range.  Uttering her words of 
magic with breathless precision, Giovanna d'Arco let fly a Holy Symbol spell.
A golden mist in the shape of a cross formed around Giovanna d'Arco.
  The Black Dragon closed to melee range, filled with uncontrolled 
blood-lust.  The Black Dragon snapped at Giovanna d'Arco but its jaws 
whiffed through the air.  Raising her hands high in the air, Giovanna d'Arco 
cast an Invisibility spell, fading into invisibility.  The Black Dragon 
lunged at its vaunted nemesis and missed.  Hoping to take advantage of a 
weak point in the Black Dragon's protection, Giovanna d'Arco thrust at 
the Black Dragon but the Black Dragon evaded the blow.
  The Black Dragon whirled about and audaciously snapped at Giovanna d'Arco 
but its jaws whiffed through the air.  Giovanna d'Arco thrust at 
the Black Dragon and damaged the Black Dragon, scoring 4 damage points.  
Giovanna d'Arco moved closer and swang at the Black Dragon but her aim was 
slightly off.  The Black Dragon snapped at Giovanna d'Arco and would have 
hit her if Giovanna d'Arco hadn't ducked just then.  Giovanna d'Arco angrily 
assailed the Black Dragon and scored 7 damage points on the Black Dragon.  
The Black Dragon acrobatically vaulted over Giovanna d'Arco and deftly 
snapped at her and missed.
  Giovanna d'Arco then swang at the Black Dragon but the Black Dragon dodged 
the blow.  The Black Dragon faked one way, then crossed over and 
treacherously snapped at Giovanna d'Arco and scorched her with 1 damage 
points.  Giovanna d'Arco shifted over for a better attacking vantage.  Then 
Giovanna d'Arco swang at the Black Dragon but her sword whiffed harmlessly 
through the air.  The Black Dragon summoned all its will and desperately 
snapped at its vaunted nemesis but its aim was slightly off the mark.
  Hoping to take advantage of a weak point in the Black Dragon's protection, 
Giovanna d'Arco skillfully thrust at the Black Dragon and scored on 
the Black Dragon, doing 5 points of damage.  The Black Dragon whirled around 
and daringly lunged at Giovanna d'Arco and would have struck her if 
Giovanna d'Arco hadn't sidestepped just then.  With surprising quickness, 
Giovanna d'Arco immediately thrust at the Black Dragon and inflicted 3 
damage points.  Undaunted, the Black Dragon moved in and snapped at 
Giovanna d'Arco and damaged her, scoring 3 damage points.  Giovanna d'Arco 
pretended to panic, then pivoted and thrust at the Black Dragon and scored 4 
damage points on the Black Dragon.  The Black Dragon circled right and 
attacked Giovanna d'Arco and missed badly.
  Giovanna d'Arco flamboyantly vaulted over the Black Dragon and deftly 
thrust at the Black Dragon but the Black Dragon evaded the blow.  
The Black Dragon turned back Giovanna d'Arco with its spirited assault.  
The Black Dragon then lunged at Giovanna d'Arco with maximum strength but 
its jaws whiffed through the air.  Giovanna d'Arco treacherously swang at 
the Black Dragon and walloped the Black Dragon with 5 damage points.  
The Black Dragon staggered, stunned by the mortal blow.  Giovanna d'Arco 
cleared out the treasure of the Black Dragon.  Giovanna d'Arco secured the 
Sword Excalibur.  She examined the Sword Excalibur and discovered the 
following properties:
  Excalibur has a +25% chance to hit and does +4 damage.  In addition, it 
confers extraordinary powers of leadership over members of the human race:  
any human army following a leader who wields Excalibur has its quality 
increased by 1 level.  Green armies become Average, Crack armies become 
Elite and so on.
  Giovanna d'Arco found 6 gold in the treasure of the Black Dragon.
  While scouting the Cavern, Giovanna d'Arco saw a Idol which seemed to be 
of a magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Idol, saying "The Idol will grant a minor Wish.  
When you scout it, you may increase any ability by one, if your unmodified 
skill level is less than your aptitude (maximum 4).  SA-y the ability number 
(0=Tactics, 1=March etc.  , the order is shown in your Character List).  
After the power of the Idol is used in a gameturn, it may not be used again 
until the next gameturn.  Hello, adventurer.  You will now be the one to 
receive my power for this year.  The Idol will grant a wish to a character.  
SA-y an ability number (not the skill name itself), and your skill shall be 
raised by one: 0-Tac, 1-Mar, 2-Nav, 3-Arc, 4-Mel, 5-Whi, 6-Nec, 7-Ele, 
8-Psy, 9-Ill, 10-Dru, 11-Thi, 12-Exp, 13-Spy, 14-Sage.  The Idol cannot 
grant the wish if the character's skill has already reached his aptitude 
level."
  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  Giovanna d'Arco moved into 
Pearlgate (#1703) with her redoubtable army.

  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Kahn (#6) (whose 
alliances are too incompatible) and Giovanna d'Arco, degrading their 
diplomatic relations 1 level(s)!
  Thus endeth the adventures of Giovanna d'Arco for this year.


  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Giovanna d'Arco 
treated with her ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Giovanna d'Arco treated 
with her ally Hokuto (#4).  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Prometeo 
(#5).  Giovanna d'Arco formally proposed a treaty with Kahn (#6), and the 
offer was accepted.  May the treaty between Giovanna d'Arco and Kahn last 
forever!
  Giovanna d'Arco treated with her ally Circe (#8).  Giovanna d'Arco treated 
with her ally Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Adhemar (#28) hiked into Chandrapur.  He had grown tired with Tesawa and 
was drawn there by rumors of its fine scotch and even more wonderful 
champagnes.
  Loviatar (#92) left Maicuru to preside over a reunion of her old regiment 
in Amberleaf.
  The 183rd Trolls grew tired of the courtesans of Marigold and moved on off 
to Maicuru where they hoped the pickings would be more to their tastes.


  Here is the financial report for Giovanna d'Arco's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 59 gold in revenue.  14 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  42 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Giovanna d'Arco was 
left with 37 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Rolando
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to spring, and I made ready to carry out my 
imperial assignments.  I marched on Moussoro (#1604) with my forces.
  With the coming of the early summer season I marched my command into 
Pearlgate (#1703).
  In late summer, I tried to improve my Tactics, but the task seemed beyond 
my aptitude.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I worked on my 
Tactics but was thwarted in my efforts.
  With the advent of the early winter season I commanded the 299th Legion, 
the 311th Legion, the 275th Legion and the 186th Legion to remain in 
Pearlgate with Giovanna d'Arco.

  Thy humble servant,   Rolando


From: Watson, Squire to Hakim
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Hakim journeyed to Marigold.  During his travels, he was 
spotted by a band of militia.  Their commanding officer suspiciously 
challenged Hakim.  But he was obviously no spy, so he got out of trouble.

  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  Hakim travelled throughout 
Marigold, exploring its features.  After his exploration efforts, 53% of it 
has been explored to date.  Hakim saw no monster.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Hakim roamed through Marigold, 
exploring the terrain there, and now 83% of it has been explored.  During 
his travels, he was ambushed, tied up and severely beaten by wild-eyed 
soldiers.  Hakim finally escaped.  A King's Marshal tracked Hakim down.  But 
when he was taken to the local sheriff, he held forth the insignia of 
Giovanna d'Arco, and was let go.

  During fall, Hakim moved into Cascadia.  He also found a Crypt (#53) in 
Cascadia, inhabited by the Basilisk.  Legend says the Ship's Log of Nautilus 
III is hidden here.  The Basilisk is a strong, 8-legged reptilian monster 
with the power to turn a man to stone with its baleful glare.  In his 
travels, he saw no monster.
  With the advent of the early winter season Hakim explored Cascadia, taking 
precise notes of the terrain and features, and now 67% of it has been 
explored.  During his travels, he was stopped by a band of militia.  Their 
commanding captain threateningly challenged Hakim.  But he was just dazzled 
by Hakim's fantastic tales of his heroism.  He saluted Hakim and marched 
away.

  Talking to some locals, Hakim heard a rumor about a Catacombs in Jadegate 
(#107), inhabited by the Renegade Priest.  Some maintain that 
the Renegade Priest actually owns the Everlasting Mistletoe.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Hakim


From: Tiffany
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I attempted a Bless spell, but bungled it.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  I cast a Clairvoyance spell 
and could see everything that happened to Guerin.  The Dry Ice Fog (an 
anti-spell Sage Discovery) seemed to lessen the effect of the Clairvoyance 
spell.
  In late summer, Tiffany's Bless spell fizzled and I wound up with my face 
covered with psycho-kinetic goo.
  The sultry days of summer surrendered to the fall.  I dropped off the 
248th Light Cavalry in Pearlgate for Drake.
  With the advent of the early winter season I was instructed in the art of 
White Magic by Drake.  I practiced my White Magic and my skill in White 
Magic went up.
  Your characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.


  Thy humble servant,   Tiffany


From: Moosu, Squire to Drake
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to fragrant spring.  Drake cast a Bless spell.  
Pearlgate was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies 
in Pearlgate.
  During early summer, Drake was instructed in the art of Meleeing by 
Giovanna d'Arco.  Drake practiced his Meleeing and improved noticeably.
  Drake heard a rumor telling of a feature in Damnonia (#1402) previously 
unknown to us, a Tomb where dwells the Ice Devil.  The Tomb is reputed to 
contain the Horn of Neptune.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer came.  Drake journeyed 
to Tigerhome.  He observed the terrain while we were on the march and now 
100% of Tigerhome has been explored.
  With the coming of the fall season, Drake moved into Pearlgate.  During 
his travels, a Witch came at Drake from out of nowhere.  He spoke to 
the Witch with friendly words, and a fight was avoided.

  During early winter, Drake tried to improve his White Magic, but the task 
was beyond his aptitude.

  Thy humble servant,   Moosu, Squire to Drake


From: Isis
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into sweet spring.  I rode into Sageleaf.  I saw no 
monsters.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I practiced enthusiastically 
and improved my skill in Element Magic.
  In late summer, I practiced my Element Magic diligently for months, but 
could make no progress.
  The summer mellowed into the fall.  I tried hard to improve my Element 
Magic, but I practiced in vain.
  With the coming of the early winter season I worked on my Element Magic 
but was frustrated in my efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Isis


From: Bairn
To: Giovanna d'Arco

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I travelled to Sageleaf.  I saw no marauding monster.
  The wet spring was followed by a sultry early summer.  I was instructed in 
the art of Element Magic by Isis.  I practiced for many weeks and my skill 
in Element Magic increased.
  With the coming of the late summer season I was instructed in Element 
Magic by Isis.  I studied and practiced my Element Magic and my skill in 
Element Magic went up.
  During fall, I practiced my Element Magic well, and even consulted a palm 
reader, but could not improve my skill in Element Magic.
  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  I tried to improve my Element 
Magic, but the task seemed beyond my ability.

  Thy humble servant,   Bairn


